[2026-03-04T20:21:52.195Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015HBRS1x1hp6K7n7KrRAgHP","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# test\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→\n     5→Runs Playwright tests for a single test file using the Replay browser, with automatic Neon\n     6→branch setup, seeding, and failed-recording upload. This is the single entry point for running\n     7→tests during development and debugging.\n     8→\n     9→## Usage\n    10→\n    11→- `package.json` entry: `\"test\": \"tsx scripts/test.ts\"`\n    12→- Required argument: a test file path (e.g., `npm run test tests/clients-list-page.spec.ts`).\n    13→- Example: `npm run test tests/auth.spec.ts`\n    14→- **Always use `npm run test`**, never `npx tsx scripts/test.ts` directly. Direct `tsx` invocation\n    15→  fails on module resolution for `@neondatabase/serverless` and other dependencies. The `npm run`\n    16→  wrapper sets up the correct resolution context.\n    17→\n    18→## Behavior\n    19→\n    20→1. **Kill stale processes**: Kill any leftover `netlify` or `vite` dev server processes from\n    21→   previous runs.\n    22→\n    23→2. **Clean up stale Neon branches**: List existing Neon branches and delete any that match the\n    24→   test branch naming convention (e.g., `test-run-*`) from interrupted previous runs.\n    25→\n    26→3. **Create ephemeral Neon branch**: Create a fresh branch from the project's main branch for\n    27→   this test run. Name it with a convention like `test-run-{timestamp}`.\n    28→\n    29→4. **Initialize and seed**: Run `initSchema` on the new branch, then run migrations, then seed\n    30→   test data.\n    31→\n    32→5. **Start `netlify dev`**: Start a single `netlify dev` instance with `DATABASE_URL` pointing\n    33→   to the ephemeral branch.\n    34→\n    35→6. **Remove stale recordings**: Run `npx replayio remove --all` to clear local recordings from\n    36→   prior runs.\n    37→\n    38→7. **Run Playwright**: Run `npx playwright test <testFile>` with `--retries 0 --workers 1`\n    39→   against the specified test file. Tests run serially, one at a time. The database is reset\n    40→   (truncate all tables and re-seed) between each test. Pipe all Playwright output to a log\n    41→   file (see Outputs).\n    42→\n    43→8. **Parse results**: Count passed/failed/skipped tests from the Playwright JSON reporter output\n    44→   at `test-results/results.json`.\n    45→\n    46→9. **On failure** (non-zero exit code):\n    47→   a. Parse `~/.replay/recordings.log` with a built-in parser (NOT `npx replayio list --json`,\n    48→      which crashes on large suites). The log is newline-delimited JSON with `kind` field:\n    49→      `createRecording`, `addMetadata`, `writeStarted`, `writeFinished`, etc.\n    50→   b. Append full metadata for every recording that has test metadata to the log file in a\n    51→      delimited block:\n    52→      ```\n    53→      === REPLAY RECORDINGS METADATA ===\n    54→      {\"id\":\"...\",\"testResult\":\"failed\",\"testTitle\":\"...\",\"specFile\":\"...\"}\n    55→      ...\n    56→      === END REPLAY RECORDINGS METADATA ===\n    57→      ```\n    58→   c. Upload exactly ONE recording: among all finished recordings where\n    59→      `metadata.test.result` is `\"failed\"` or `\"timedOut\"`, pick the one with the longest\n    60→      duration (the real recording, not zero-duration stubs). Upload with\n    61→      `npx replayio upload <id>`. On success, append `REPLAY UPLOADED: <recordingId>` to the\n    62→      log file. On failure, log the exit code.\n    63→\n    64→10. **Clean up**: Stop the `netlify dev` server. Delete the ephemeral Neon branch. Remove local\n    65→    recordings with `npx replayio remove --all`.\n    66→\n    67→11. **Print summary** to stdout: a single line like `10 passed` or\n    68→    `8 passed, 2 failed — see logs/test-run-3.log`. Include the uploaded recording ID\n    69→    if one was uploaded: `8 passed, 2 failed (recording: abc123) — see logs/test-run-3.log`.\n    70→\n    71→12. **Exit** with the original Playwright exit code.\n    72→\n    73→## Inputs\n    74→\n    75→- **Required argument**: Test file path (e.g., `tests/auth.spec.ts`).\n    76→- **Environment variables**:\n    77→  - `NEON_API_KEY` (required): For Neon branch management.\n    78→  - `RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY` (required): For Replay recording uploads.\n    79→  - `NEON_PROJECT_ID` (required): Read from `.env`. The Neon project to branch from.\n    80→  - `DATABASE_URL` (required): Read from `.env`. The main branch connection string used as\n    81→    template for ephemeral branches.\n    82→  - `REPLAY_CLI` (optional): Override the Replay CLI command (default: `replayio`, assumed\n    83→    globally installed). Useful for pointing at a local build or alternate installation.\n    84→- **Files**:\n    85→  - `.env`: Project configuration (Neon project ID, database URL, etc.).\n    86→  - `~/.replay/recordings.log`: Replay recording metadata (read after test run).\n    87→\n    88→## Outputs\n    89→\n    90→- **stdout**: One-line summary only. Never verbose test output.\n    91→- **`logs/test-run-N.log`**: Full Playwright output, recording metadata, and upload results.\n    92→  `N` increments each run (find the highest existing number and add 1).\n    93→- **Side effects**:\n    94→  - Creates and deletes ephemeral Neon branches.\n    95→  - Uploads failed Replay recordings.\n    96→  - Removes local recording files.\n    97→- **Exit codes**:\n    98→  - 0: All tests passed.\n    99→  - Non-zero: Test failures (matches Playwright's exit code).\n   100→\n   101→## Implementation Tips\n   102→\n   103→- Reuse `initSchema` from `scripts/schema.ts` and the seed logic from `scripts/seed-db.ts`.\n   104→- Use the Neon API directly (`fetch` to `https://console.neon.tech/api/v2/...`) for branch\n   105→  creation and deletion. The API key is `NEON_API_KEY`.\n   106→- Parse `~/.replay/recordings.log` in TypeScript — it's newline-delimited JSON. The\n   107→  `addMetadata` entries contain `metadata.test.result` which indicates pass/fail.\n   108→- The Playwright config must use the Replay browser via `replayDevices['Replay Chromium']`\n   109→  from `@replayio/playwright` and include `replayReporter` with `upload: false`.\n   110→- The HTML reporter must use `open: 'never'` to suppress the interactive \"Serving HTML report\"\n   111→  prompt that blocks the script from exiting.\n   112→- Run Playwright with `--retries 0 --workers 1` — no retries, no parallelism. Failures must\n   113→  be analyzed via Replay.\n   114→- Do NOT inherit stdio from Playwright. Pipe stdout and stderr to the log file using\n   115→  `child_process.execSync` with `stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe']` or similar, then write\n   116→  the captured output to the log file.\n   117→- Use the JSON reporter (`test-results/results.json`) to parse pass/fail counts for the\n   118→  summary line.\n   119→- The `RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY` env var is already set in the container.\n   120→- Reset the database between tests by truncating all app tables and re-running the seed script.\n   121→  This ensures each test starts with a clean, known dataset.\n   122→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BpZQ7ru5ReeTrZZBiaxgTP","session_id":"3e708823-920f-43f5-b295-766b5a5c6f26","uuid":"fe3696ab-61bc-46a7-aec5-9761a29d2b1e"}
[2026-03-04T20:21:52.206Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01AZW5r1FSQjdrSnS3LsUXWP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P2YvGJZXmpUmrKJM2t5Wy8","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/repo/apps/todo-app/AppSpec.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":445,"cache_read_input_tokens":28893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":445,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BpZQ7ru5ReeTrZZBiaxgTP","session_id":"3e708823-920f-43f5-b295-766b5a5c6f26","uuid":"dbded99c-f00b-4b62-9bea-44e865dda0b8"}
[2026-03-04T20:21:52.389Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P2YvGJZXmpUmrKJM2t5Wy8","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Todo App\n     2→\n     3→A clean, modern task management application that lets users create, organize, and track their todos.\n     4→\n     5→## Pages\n     6→\n     7→### 1. Main Todo List Page (`/`)\n     8→\n     9→The primary page of the app. Shows all todos with filtering and creation capabilities.\n    10→\n    11→#### Header\n    12→- App title \"Todo App\" displayed at the top left\n    13→- A count of incomplete todos shown (e.g., \"3 items left\")\n    14→\n    15→#### Add Todo\n    16→- A text input at the top with placeholder \"What needs to be done?\"\n    17→- Pressing Enter with non-empty text creates a new todo and clears the input\n    18→- New todos are added to the top of the list with status \"active\" (not completed)\n    19→\n    20→#### Todo List\n    21→- Each todo item displays:\n    22→  - A checkbox on the left to toggle completion\n    23→  - The todo text in the center\n    24→  - A priority badge (Low, Medium, High) shown as a colored tag\n    25→  - A due date (if set), displayed relative to today (e.g., \"Today\", \"Tomorrow\", \"Overdue\")\n    26→  - A delete button (trash icon) on the right, visible on hover\n    27→- Completed todos have strikethrough text styling and reduced opacity\n    28→- Clicking the todo text opens the Edit Todo Modal\n    29→- Checking/unchecking the checkbox toggles the completed status and persists to the database\n    30→- Clicking the delete button removes the todo after a confirmation prompt\n    31→\n    32→#### Filters\n    33→- Filter bar below the input with buttons: \"All\", \"Active\", \"Completed\"\n    34→- The currently selected filter is visually highlighted\n    35→- \"All\" shows all todos (default)\n    36→- \"Active\" shows only incomplete todos\n    37→- \"Completed\" shows only completed todos\n    38→- A \"Clear Completed\" button on the right side removes all completed todos\n    39→\n    40→#### Sorting\n    41→- A dropdown to sort by: \"Newest First\" (default), \"Oldest First\", \"Priority\", \"Due Date\"\n    42→\n    43→### 2. Edit Todo Modal\n    44→\n    45→A modal dialog that opens when clicking a todo item's text.\n    46→\n    47→#### Fields\n    48→- **Title**: Text input, pre-filled with current todo text (required)\n    49→- **Priority**: Dropdown selector with options: Low, Medium, High (default: Medium)\n    50→- **Due Date**: Date picker input (optional)\n    51→- **Notes**: Multiline textarea for additional details (optional)\n    52→\n    53→#### Actions\n    54→- \"Save\" button: Saves changes and closes the modal\n    55→- \"Cancel\" button: Discards changes and closes the modal\n    56→- Clicking outside the modal also closes it (discarding changes)\n    57→\n    58→## Data Model\n    59→\n    60→### Todo\n    61→| Field       | Type      | Description                          |\n    62→|-------------|-----------|--------------------------------------|\n    63→| id          | UUID      | Primary key                          |\n    64→| title       | TEXT      | The todo item text (required)        |\n    65→| completed   | BOOLEAN   | Whether the todo is done             |\n    66→| priority    | TEXT      | \"low\", \"medium\", or \"high\"           |\n    67→| due_date    | DATE      | Optional due date                    |\n    68→| notes       | TEXT      | Optional additional notes            |\n    69→| created_at  | TIMESTAMP | When the todo was created            |\n    70→| updated_at  | TIMESTAMP | When the todo was last modified      |\n    71→\n    72→## API Endpoints\n    73→\n    74→### `GET /.netlify/functions/todos`\n    75→Returns all todos, sorted by `created_at` descending.\n    76→\n    77→### `POST /.netlify/functions/todos`\n    78→Creates a new todo. Body: `{ title, priority?, due_date?, notes? }`\n    79→\n    80→### `PUT /.netlify/functions/todos/:id`\n    81→Updates an existing todo. Body: partial todo fields.\n    82→\n    83→### `DELETE /.netlify/functions/todos/:id`\n    84→Deletes a todo by ID.\n    85→\n    86→### `DELETE /.netlify/functions/todos?completed=true`\n    87→Deletes all completed todos (\"Clear Completed\" action).\n    88→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BpZQ7ru5ReeTrZZBiaxgTP","session_id":"3e708823-920f-43f5-b295-766b5a5c6f26","uuid":"5b5e26fd-fa87-42ca-9d78-ee38d8ae9e94"}
